                        "review": "I played this on the Oculus Rift with Touch Controllers.  I had a roomscale setup.  I played on the realistic setting.  So this game is exactly what it sounds like.  You are skiing on a pre-determined track and then jump.  You crouch down while you're going downhill and then stand up when you want to jump to get the maximum distance.  I think you're also supposed to align your skis in a certain way to increase the distance.  \n\nThere are no trick jumps (yet).  There is no skiing outside the predetermined rails.  You can change the skis you have on in the ski shop.  If you look at the store description video, that's exactly what you're getting.  No more, no less.  \n\nShould you get this game?  Tough call.  There's just not a lot of gameplay here really.  You can get a nice workout from having to crouch down and then stand up multiple times.  There's the challenge of trying to climb up the leaderboards.  There's just not a lot of variety.  I'll give a tepid recommendation due to the low price and because the videos are pretty accurate about what you're getting.  Make sure this game is for you.\n\nRating 5/10 I think I had fun, did I?  Maybe, I don't know.  Would love to see trick jumps added.  At least maybe facials if you don't land properly.",
